{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793693500,"nonce":"uba36czxLq05oqzHMYPrSYhqtS0=","message":"Where method_call's time goes, NUC release, 4 CPUs, wall 48 ms (CI: 87 ms against LuaJIT 8.4 ms). Runtime init about 7 ms (hello world 6.7), lowering and module compile 12, then the main thread waits 21.8 ms for lua$chunk's compile (trace: '? waited 21.84 ms for bead 133'; body 18.2 of 23.4, the pipeline's own passes 15.4 ms in 4 rounds, no pass above 2 ms: error_flag 1.9, drop_insert 1.4, inline 1.5 over three rounds, heap_scalarize 1.1, aggregate_scalarize 0.8), then about 6.6 ms of one-at-a-time first-call baseline compiles of the 12 small functions the chunk calls, then about 2 ms of compute. The cause is the size of the lowered chunk: 4,965 lines, 766 blocks (629 branches), 225 calls for about 45 statements, 2,878 lines and 412 blocks after the pipeline. Per call site the lowering emits both candidate targets (lua$Toggle$activate$3 and lua$NthToggle$activate$5, 20 calls each) and cold error paths in line (zl_index_nil 51, zl_annotate 32, zl_raise_call_nil 20). Tried: ZYNTAX_COMPILE_WORKERS=2 and 3 moves wall 48.2 to 47.8 and 47.3 ms (the callees are asked for at their first call, so extra workers have nothing to run). Not a fix: interpreting the chunk first, because the program thread's wait moves into the timed region (the timer starts at the top of the chunk), trading the cold column for the warm one. Ash is not a template for this part: its default policy (ASH_AIR_INTERP_POLICY=backedge) also prepares a loop-carrying function at full price, and its demand policy is documented as losing OSR for a main called once, which is this shape; its method_call is 100M vtable dispatches against our 4M calls. Directions: emit less IR per method call (shared out-of-line cold paths, one target per site when the shape is known), ask for the callees when the chunk's compile is asked for, and the start-up floor. Even then method_call cannot reach 2x LuaJIT by wall: that is 17 ms and the CI start-up floor alone is 13 to 20 ms.","files":null}]}